: $6.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 4K people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 13%/yr across its filed history. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Digital Realty Trust, Inc. is a large-cap real estate business with a $62.5B market cap on $6.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +13% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 149% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.4941484797632325},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Among the least levered in Real Estate \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Real Estate sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Landscape Capital Management L.L.C. Makes New Investment in Digital Realty Trust, Inc. $DLR","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/20/landscape-capital-management-l-l-c-makes-new-investment-in-digital-realty-trust-inc-dlr.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795176049.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.957,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Are Record Bookings Lifting Guidance at Digital Realty (NYSE:DLR)?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/infrastructure-and-real-estate/how-are-record-bookings-lifting-guidance-at-digital-realty-nysedlr","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795155000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Why (DLR) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/20/Why_DLR_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_T